# L §5.18 example ask q6, copied: readers-of x is "every item that reads x, directly or not: defs, fills, moves,
# regimes' items and asks, each once, the direct readers first, then by depth, then by id".  rent reads rent_amt;
# budget reads rent; asks a1 (reads budget) and a2 (reads rent_amt).  Depth 1: a2, rent; depth 2: budget; depth 3: a1.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input rent_amt[m in months]: money PLN

def rent[m in months]: money PLN = rent_amt[m] at start_of(m)
def budget[m in months]: money PLN = rent[m] at start_of(m)

ask a1: budget[2026-03]
ask a2: rent_amt[2026-03]
ask q6: readers-of rent_amt
=== expect q6
q6: a2, rent, budget, a1
